[{:db/id 17592186166933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7ee61787-7fd7-52ae-8d70-3b4f4209ed09" "question-66762fbf-e11e-5167-966c-39877463d24c" "question-78263033-1bff-5da3-9201-fff7488d909f" "question-53078cf1-e2a6-5757-9214-0bb6642d4a23"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166530 :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f593c497549ccb07e43a985e77b35b313421eb1194143ad35e7d06a2c0bbe3a.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, find the system of equations." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\}-3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+2L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\cos(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{s}{s^2+4}, \\quad\n\\mathcal L\\{\\sin(2t)\\} = \\dfrac{2}{s^2+4},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+4}-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+2=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" "question-1151a388-649e-5c91-8e65-af0ed8268c10" "question-8dcb1599-ae92-594f-a29c-09dd73cb7136" "question-4e326d04-8454-5a4c-8291-8ce0cd1c8852"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166531 :question/problem "![](images/b8/b8fb674be80033481557f5d18625e9d406934b0702f21997fcdd544ab92691ba.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$  find the solution of the new system." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-0=2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\},$ and we have used the fact that $\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac1s.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+3){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+4}{s(s+1)}) \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\dfrac{s+4}{s(s+1)} ,\\qquad \nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2(s+4)}{s(s+1)(s+3)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166935 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-81e3b89d-a932-5551-882e-cf97243e80bc" "question-69e91785-0e6d-5932-8b31-7b7666b19d7a" "question-80182570-5c16-548e-a977-c22b33e10f6d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166532 :question/problem "![](images/61/61e3df899d4d41b388f160da60691aab05bd396f9826e0ea11db32780ff1ce55.svg)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} = -\\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{2}{s-1} - \\dfrac{2}{s}, \\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s+2} + \\dfrac{3}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." :question/worked-solution "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{2}{s-1}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+2}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{1\\cdot t}-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+2}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t}-{e}^{-2t}-2 \\\\ {e}^{-2t}+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ee61787-7fd7-52ae-8d70-3b4f4209ed09" :question/id #uuid "7ee61787-7fd7-52ae-8d70-3b4f4209ed09" :question/math-academy-id "q-332827" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={{field-1}} \\\\ {{field-2}}=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-5L\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+2L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,L\\{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8055394-ff54-59e8-97af-e59ec5d57577" "answer-field-310c7a56-5779-5193-ba63-3d051a163d7b" "answer-field-47cd9c17-da01-57dd-b7a4-e1e589cf3c59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8055394-ff54-59e8-97af-e59ec5d57577" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8055394-ff54-59e8-97af-e59ec5d57577" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-276559b7-acce-5afc-8493-8fd35dab3650" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f342f7d-f1a7-517d-9ceb-fa32f8e654c0" "answer-5e5a58fc-5744-57b6-9455-edc920e17333" "answer-276559b7-acce-5afc-8493-8fd35dab3650" "answer-d0808cce-237e-5b98-ac4f-919a009b9a9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f342f7d-f1a7-517d-9ceb-fa32f8e654c0" :answer/id #uuid "0f342f7d-f1a7-517d-9ceb-fa32f8e654c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e5a58fc-5744-57b6-9455-edc920e17333" :answer/id #uuid "5e5a58fc-5744-57b6-9455-edc920e17333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-276559b7-acce-5afc-8493-8fd35dab3650" :answer/id #uuid "276559b7-acce-5afc-8493-8fd35dab3650" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{5s}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0808cce-237e-5b98-ac4f-919a009b9a9e" :answer/id #uuid "d0808cce-237e-5b98-ac4f-919a009b9a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-310c7a56-5779-5193-ba63-3d051a163d7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "310c7a56-5779-5193-ba63-3d051a163d7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1b7a2bd7-9605-5038-a6aa-2bd7a389479f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b7a2bd7-9605-5038-a6aa-2bd7a389479f" "answer-a6c1bbeb-8d1d-5bfb-84a6-750229aefdcb" "answer-5fe9e4c2-6857-5e76-a5e1-c934b2