/id #uuid "e723be1e-3436-5f1e-ae9b-8aed6f8e9333" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-53078cf1-e2a6-5757-9214-0bb6642d4a23" :question/id #uuid "53078cf1-e2a6-5757-9214-0bb6642d4a23" :question/math-academy-id "q-332815" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+{t}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={{field-1}}-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ {{field-2}}={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+{t}^{2}-4\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{t}^{2}\\}-4L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the results\n\n$$\nL\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s},\\,L\\{{t}^{2}\\}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\n$$\n\n we can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0bcd9933-4565-5008-bc52-ad3b38e3f88d" "answer-field-35386b35-cbdb-5ebe-a7a2-329af540e261" "answer-field-63739b3b-c806-54f1-82df-80124eca0140"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0bcd9933-4565-5008-bc52-ad3b38e3f88d" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bcd9933-4565-5008-bc52-ad3b38e3f88d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-356f21fe-a1c7-5137-8d1b-2746f4b08fb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e18df4c6-9fa8-5d8a-a157-1c59373bfda9" "answer-5fe66e76-0d0f-5d26-8ee9-b827b97e4539" "answer-356f21fe-a1c7-5137-8d1b-2746f4b08fb7" "answer-6579df18-faf4-5454-8272-7e532385de39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e18df4c6-9fa8-5d8a-a157-1c59373bfda9" :answer/id #uuid "e18df4c6-9fa8-5d8a-a157-1c59373bfda9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fe66e76-0d0f-5d26-8ee9-b827b97e4539" :answer/id #uuid "5fe66e76-0d0f-5d26-8ee9-b827b97e4539" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-356f21fe-a1c7-5137-8d1b-2746f4b08fb7" :answer/id #uuid "356f21fe-a1c7-5137-8d1b-2746f4b08fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6579df18-faf4-5454-8272-7e532385de39" :answer/id #uuid "6579df18-faf4-5454-8272-7e532385de39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{4}{{s}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35386b35-cbdb-5ebe-a7a2-329af540e261" :answer-field/id #uuid "35386b35-cbdb-5ebe-a7a2-329af540e261" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e9855f71-3925-56d1-a713-67c0c675857a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a19e395e-0913-5f46-8f69-6e5b6dfd5c17" "answer-e9855f71-3925-56d1-a713-67c0c675857a" "answer-440d62ed-bf39-5eaf-8209-95ed197f8e99" "answer-5356ff5e-636f-58d4-92d2-a4ff67a86e6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a19e395e-0913-5f46-8f69-6e5b6dfd5c17" :answer/id #uuid "a19e395e-0913-5f46-8f69-6e5b6dfd5c17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9855f71-3925-56d1-a713-67c0c675857a" :answer/id #uuid "e9855f71-3925-56d1-a713-67c0c675857a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-440d62ed-bf39-5eaf-8209-95ed197f8e99" :answer/id #uuid "440d62ed-bf39-5eaf-8209-95ed197f8e99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{2}(s)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5356ff5e-636f-58d4-92d2-a4ff67a86e6b" :answer/id #uuid "5356ff5e-636f-58d4-92d2-a4ff67a86e6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{X}_{2}(s)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-63739b3b-c806-54f1-82df-80124eca0140" :answer-field/id #uuid "63739b3b-c806-54f1-82df-80124eca0140" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8967beff-6a3f-5bb3-915e-81326469bd26" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fc2895b-f315-5f9d-b618-510679fe6a62" "answer-aa50de8e-6800-5f19-b5fc-984a07017bdc" "answer-8967beff-6a3f-5bb3-915e-81326469bd26" "answer-7b23bee2-047e-5a60-893b-cf231a6060e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fc2895b-f315-5f9d-b618-510679fe6a62" :answer/id #uuid "6fc2895b-f315-5f9d-b618-510679fe6a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa50de8e-6800-5f19-b5fc-984a07017bdc" :answer/id #uuid "aa50de8e-6800-5f19-b5fc-984a07017bdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8967beff-6a3f-5bb3-915e-81326469bd26" :answer/id #uuid "8967beff-6a3f-5bb3-915e-81326469bd26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b23bee2-047e-5a60-893b-cf231a6060e8" :answer/id #uuid "7b23bee2-047e-5a60-893b-cf231a6060e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186305119 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+5\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1=2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s+1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =2(\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)})-1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2(s+5)-s(s+1)}{s(s+1)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s+1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186304448 :answer-field/correct "answer-f9672cef-bf4e-59e9-b645-aca152e48467" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f9672cef-bf4e-59e9-b645-aca152e48467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9672cef-bf4e-59e9-b645-aca152e48467" :answer/id #uuid "f9672cef-bf4e-59e9-b645-aca152e48467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-s^{2}+s+10}{s(s+1)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" :question/id #uuid "b4ba1928-c543-554d-8f81-96f348be498a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333055" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-2\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1-\\frac{2}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(1+\\frac{2}{s}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-(\\frac{s+2}{s}) \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-4 & =2{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2{X}_{1}(s)+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =2(-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)})+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{2(s+2)}{s(s-3)}+4 \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2(s+2)+4s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s-4+4{s}^{2}-12s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-5){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c5489e0-fc0c-5c3d-9e36-b3584f966d21"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c5489e0-fc0c-5c3d-9e36-b3584f966d21" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5489e0-fc0c-5c3d-9e36-b3584f966d21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1" :answer/id #uuid "2d856e13-fac1-552c-8875-d611da9c00a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{s}^{2}-14s-4}{s(s-3)(s-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1151a388-649e-5c91-8e65-af0ed8268c10" :question/id #uuid "1151a388-649e-5c91-8e65-af0ed8268c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-333068" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-(\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-2)-(s+5)}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-2s)-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-4s-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7711698c-a576-5c6f-98d2-825afa236b73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7711698c-a576-5c6f-98d2-825afa236b73" :answer-field/id #uuid "7711698c-a576-5c6f-98d2-825afa236b73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e" :answer/id #uuid "7107643e-b101-593c-a4be-aed821d14b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8dcb1599-ae92-594f-a29c-09dd73cb7136" :question/id #uuid "8dcb1599-ae92-594f-a29c-09dd73cb7136" :question/math-academy-id "q-332785" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1=3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & =3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =-1 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2{X}_{1}(s)+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =-2(-\\frac{1}{s-3})+2+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =(\\frac{2}{s-3})+(\\frac{2s+3}{s}) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2s+3)(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+(2{s}^{2}-3s-9)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6a42c68c-d4e8-5983-b007-8f6d9f9201ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a42c68c-d4e8-5983-b007-8f6d9f9201ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a42c68c-d4e8-5983-b007-8f6d9f9201ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ff1cca40-79b7-5eb7-83aa-4e7f56ba740f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff1cca40-79b7-5eb7-83aa-4e7f56ba740f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff1cca40-79b7-5eb7-83aa-4e7f56ba740f" :answer/id #uuid "ff1cca40-79b7-5eb7-83aa-4e7f56ba740f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{s}^{2}-s-9}{s(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4e326d04-8454-5a4c-8291-8ce0cd1c8852" :question/id #uuid "4e326d04-8454-5a4c-8291-8ce0cd1c8852" :question/math-academy-id "q-333061" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3 & =-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s+2){X}_{1}(s) & =-3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =-\\frac{3}{s+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3{X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}+1 \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =3(-\\frac{3}{s+2})+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9}{s+2}+\\frac{5+s}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-\\frac{9s}{s(s+2)}+\\frac{(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+(5+s)(s+2)}{s(s+2)} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-9s+5s+{s}^{2}+10+2s}{s(s+2)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-337d0577-b7fc-523e-8b76-50488544ecf7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-337d0577-b7fc-523e-8b76-50488544ecf7" :answer-field/id #uuid "337d0577-b7fc-523e-8b76-50488544ecf7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0" :answer/id #uuid "7b58a5cd-7ca6-5b39-aacf-b77684b7ded0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s^{2}-2s+10}{s(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308392 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)-20 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s+2}+\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+2}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\cdot t}+3{e}^{1\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-1+2{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308320 :answer-field/correct "answer-efb58fda-6ca6-5393-9496-b15960faa397" :answer-field/choices ["answer-efb58fda-6ca6-5393-9496-b15960faa397"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efb58fda-6ca6-5393-9496-b15960faa397" :answer/id #uuid "efb58fda-6ca6-5393-9496-b15960faa397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{-2t}+3e^{t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186307916 :answer-field/correct "answer-73ee6fcd-d6ef-50ab-ae3b-4fd13493375b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73ee6fcd-d6ef-50ab-ae3b-4fd13493375b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73ee6fcd-d6ef-50ab-ae3b-4fd13493375b" :answer/id #uuid "73ee6fcd-d6ef-50ab-ae3b-4fd13493375b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-81e3b89d-a932-5551-882e-cf97243e80bc" :question/id #uuid "81e3b89d-a932-5551-882e-cf97243e80bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-333129" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{3}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-3{e}^{1\\cdot t}+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t}+1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-150cc971-a84f-524e-85be-4ba5c139cbb9" "answer-field-b24e4e2e-0f9e-5dca-ba9f-d39c3d172355"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-150cc971-a84f-524e-85be-4ba5c139cbb9" :answer-field/id #uuid "150cc971-a84f-524e-85be-4ba5c139cbb9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec" :answer/id #uuid "33b80eef-df10-542e-9407-86feef4fb7ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{3t}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b24e4e2e-0f9e-5dca-ba9f-d39c3d172355" :answer-field/id #uuid "b24e4e2e-0f9e-5dca-ba9f-d39c3d172355" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929" :answer/id #uuid "6ca7bb14-8c09-5fbf-9824-91b12b83b929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3t}-3{e}^{t}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-69e91785-0e6d-5932-8b31-7b7666b19d7a" :question/id #uuid "69e91785-0e6d-5932-8b31-7b7666b19d7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-333136" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+{e}^{3\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{1\\cdot t}+1 \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{t}-1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t}+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-64259115-8467-5355-9ba3-628dcd4e0781" "answer-field-f09a48b6-6147-5c33-8f73-ea1439dfbd04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-64259115-8467-5355-9ba3-628dcd4e0781" :answer-field/id #uuid "64259115-8467-5355-9ba3-628dcd4e0781" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fe5816cf-57c0-58c1-b85d-cb4c08ed65b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe5816cf-57c0-58c1-b85d-cb4c08ed65b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe5816cf-57c0-58c1-b85d-cb4c08ed65b1" :answer/id #uuid "fe5816cf-57c0-58c1-b85d-cb4c08ed65b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+e^{3t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f09a48b6-6147-5c33-8f73-ea1439dfbd04" :answer-field/id #uuid "f09a48b6-6147-5c33-8f73-ea1439dfbd04" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-94645582-a111-50c2-9426-8d1ed31b5cb4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94645582-a111-50c2-9426-8d1ed31b5cb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94645582-a111-50c2-9426-8d1ed31b5cb4" :answer/id #uuid "94645582-a111-50c2-9426-8d1ed31b5cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{t}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-80182570-5c16-548e-a977-c22b33e10f6d" :question/id #uuid "80182570-5c16-548e-a977-c22b33e10f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-333124" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)-3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}-1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-3 \\\\ {e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-269c3ef7-1f7e-5b5b-b5b6-94fa2ab0a45d" "answer-field-df9aae05-0903-5349-afc8-277fbc48692c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-269c3ef7-1f7e-5b5b-b5b6-94fa2ab0a45d" :answer-field/id #uuid "269c3ef7-1f7e-5b5b-b5b6-94fa2ab0a45d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e" :answer/id #uuid "2231d8eb-43c8-5010-a3d6-0228d639d76e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-df9aae05-0903-5349-afc8-277fbc48692c" :answer-field/id #uuid "df9aae05-0903-5349-afc8-277fbc48692c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018" :answer/id #uuid "9d746ceb-03b3-5401-ab18-45b6c0ecc018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167233 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+6,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{2}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{1\\cdot t}+2{e}^{3\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{t}+2{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\}-2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\cdot t}-2 \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t}+{e}^{t}-1 \\\\ {e}^{3t}-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164464 :answer-field/correct "answer-c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7" :answer/id #uuid "c2fe2a56-87fa-54f1-8bda-525eba574bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{t}+2e^{3t}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164465 :answer-field/correct "answer-a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389" :answer/id #uuid "a22272d0-9fb6-5234-800e-83cf913bd389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{3t}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168032 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve inhomogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/e0/e04825ebe3b670d020df9c4dad9b86564a57542effc88b77d5778f535e15d5bf.svg)\n\nSimilar to the homogeneous case, the process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find initial variables \n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167993 :tutorial/content "![](images/0b/0bebe0003d3d70b77be931f2dba651d85352bddf6e41b94055bb227b07d60153.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+5\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)-2\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-2L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the result\n\n$$\n\\mathcal L\\{1\\} = \\dfrac{1}{s},\n$$\n\nwe can write our system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)-\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively.\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) - 3 = - 2 \\left(\\dfrac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}\\right) + 4 X_2(s) - \\dfrac{2}{s}\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{3s^2-s-8}{s(s-1)(s-4)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{-2s+5}{s(s-1)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s-1}-\\frac{5}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}-5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =3{e}^{t}-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3{s}^{2}-s-8}{s(s-1)(s-4)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{3}{s-4}-\\frac{2}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-1}\\}+3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-4}\\}-2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}+3{e}^{4t}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{t}-5 \\\\ 2{e}^{t}+3{e}^{4t}-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166988 :activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
